t has one slider I can take  the slider and I can drag the slider and  I can see my content change  appropriately so this was built for  touchscreens which means we needed to do  a few things differently things like  Mouse position don't make a whole lot of  sense in this case but we do have a new  function called touch position which  makes more sense and mouse position sort  supports one point because we only ever  have one Mouse on these desktop and  laptop computers  whereas on touchscreens I can have 10  possibly more points and so if I put my  finger on the screen if I put two down I  get two points in three and four and  five and I can just keep putting more  fingers down on the screen and get some  more points for that so you can do some  interesting things with the new touch  position function and if you need to do  something custom with the layout of  manipulate controls we support some new  functionality there as well if you have  controls that are very tall for example  and you don't necessarily want them at  the bottom of the screen because maybe  it would take up too much vertical space  we have a new option to manipulate  called touch screen control placement  and you can  move the touchscreen controls to  different sides of the screen so in this  case I have a vertical slider and rather  than taking up all of the space at the  bottom for this very tall thin thing I  just moved it over to the right side and  so here's my manipulate my controls are  over on the right side I have this  vertical slider and I can slide this and  the manipulate controls aren't covering  very much of the screen so I'll talk  real quick about the limitations some of  the limitations of this product as I  mentioned earlier it supports read-only  documents you cannot create new  documents you cannot edit documents this  is a player product wolfram player if  you want to create and edit documents on  an iPad we do have an app that's already  available called Wolfram cloud that 